# This repository is published to GitHub Pages, so its working directory is a
# public directory with a delay. Anything listed here is something that must
# never survive a careless `git add -A`.

# --- credentials -------------------------------------------------------------
# A helper-store file sits in this working directory. It has never been pushed
# and it must never be. It is listed first because it is the only entry here
# whose absence would be a security incident rather than noise.
.git-credentials
.git-credentials.*
.netrc
.env
.env.*

# --- mount artifacts ---------------------------------------------------------
# The repo is edited over a FUSE mount, which leaves a .fuse_hidden* stub
# beside every file that is rewritten while something still holds it open.
# They are byte copies of real pages, so committing one publishes a stale
# duplicate of a live page under a garbage name.
.fuse_hidden*

# --- local tool output -------------------------------------------------------
# Browser evidence for UI work. Screenshots are large, regenerated on demand
# and meaningless to a visitor.
.playwright-mcp/
# Design-tooling hook cache, per checkout.
.impeccable/

# --- scratch copies of the single sources of truth ----------------------------
# assets/brand.css and index.html are the only places the ecosystem styles and
# script are allowed to live; see the build rule in assets/brand_inline.py and
# assets/eco_build.py. These two files are unreferenced extracts of those
# blocks, kept by hand while working and stale the moment either source moves.
# Ignoring them keeps a second, silently divergent copy out of the repository.
assets/_eco_css.txt
assets/_eco_script.js

# --- editor and OS noise -----------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
# Local dev server config for the preview pane. Points at an absolute path on
# one machine and a port on one machine, so it is useless to anyone else and
# would only ever conflict.
.claude/launch.json

# --- python bytecode ---------------------------------------------------------
# The build scripts under assets/ are stdlib Python and are meant to be read.
# Their bytecode is not.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
